Since pd.solve() checks whether matrices are symmetric and positive definite, I added checks as well for the D3 test.  NPD throws an informative error about which matrix was the problem, but in the instance of non-symmetry (which would make no sense, so it must be a machine-precision issue), I try iteratively rounding the matrix to 15, 14, 13, ... no less than 3 decimal places before using it to calculate log-likelihoods.  Could you please install the latest development version of semTools (0.4-15.906) and try testing these again?

devtools::install_github("simsem/semTools/semTools")

You should see more informative messages this time.  And what's more, as long as the matrix causing the error was approximately symmetric, you should get a D3 test statistic (along with a message saying how much rounding was required to do so).

Please let me know how it goes.  Thanks,

