> The only difference between two models are the position of "attacking" in #regression equation.

That is unexpected.  Could you post some data to reproduce the problem?  You could also compare the parameter tables

PT6 <- lavaanify(model6, auto = TRUE)
PT7 <- lavaanify(model7, auto = TRUE)

By the way, this is problematic:

    #residual correlations
      value     ~~ 1*value
      rating    ~~ 1*rating

You are not specifying correlations, you are fixing residual variances to 1.  That is too restrictive because you are also fixing the first factor loading of each of those constructs to 1 (std.lv <http://std.lv> = FALSE implies that, check your parameter table or summary() output).  Since value is regressed on rating, you cannot additionally estimate a residual covariance/correlation anyway, and fixing it to a nonzero value would just attenuate the estimate of the regression slope value~rating.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
