Dear all,
I am having some issues using an imputed dataset (created with MICE) with lavaan.mi.  I am definitely doing something wrong when creating the dataset list, so I was wondering if you could help me locating the source of the error and perhaps point me to some reference/explanation.

So, If I impute a dataset (I use defaults in this example)

impcos <- mice(cos, m = 20, diagnostics = TRUE)

then do this

dat <- complete(impcos, 'long', inc=TRUE)

and then
fit <- cfa.mi(COS.mi, data = dat$imp, estimator = "MLM", chi="all")

I receive an error stating that data is not a valid input type. I have tried a lot of different combinations but nothing. I am sure it is something very basic and obvious, but how do create an object with MICE that can be used with lavaan.mi?

Also, (not related to lavaan.mi) once the dataset list is created how do I save it as a .rdata file?

Is this the right function to do so?

write.mice.imputation(mi.res= impcos , name="impcos" )

Thanks very much

Giovanni

